      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the current climate, absolute political \"neutrality\" often *is* interpreted as a moral or ethical endorsement of the status quo, which is a very strong accusation in the modern discourse.\n\nChoosing to support the *ethical framework* the Act promotes is not always the same as \"picking a political side,\" but it is a definitive **position on the topic of corporate responsibility and environment first and foremost for the brand and the market to see it clearly.\n\nTherefore, to win the \"moral high ground\" in the eyes of the demanding modern consumer, **a strong, values-driven commitment to the *substance* of the regulation is generally the more powerful and \"safe\" narrative to control right now, rather than the *opinion* of the political debate around it",
